app.listen(port, () => console.log(`Server running on port ${port}`));
```

This sets up a basic Express server with a route that responds with "Hello World!".

7. Create a new file called `.env` (without any file extension) in your project root and add the following contents:

```
PORT=3000
```

This sets a default port to use when running your server.

8. Create a new file called `package.json` (if it doesn't exist already) and add the following contents:

```json
{
  "scripts": {
    "start": "nodemon",
    "watch": "tsc -watch",
    "dev": "concurrently \"npm run watch\" \"npm start\""
  }
}
```

This sets up three main commands:

- `start` runs `nodemon`, which automatically restarts your server when TypeScript files change.
- `watch` runs the TypeScript compiler in watch mode to compile changes in your TypeScript files.
- `dev` runs both `watch` and `start` commands concurrently.

