As for the history and development of these operating systems:

**Windows 10**

Windows 10 was officially announced on September 30, 2014, and launched on July 29, 2015. It is the fifth major release by Microsoft under the Windows NT family, following Windows 8.1, and is designed to run applications written in various programming languages, both classic and modern. Windows 10 received several updates since its release, each bringing improvements to performance, security, and feature enhancements.

**Ubuntu 20.04**

Ubuntu 20.04 LTS (Focal Fossa) was released on April 23, 2020. It is based on the Linux kernel version 5.4 and includes the GNOME v3.36.1 desktop environment. The operating system is known for its strong emphasis on security, performance, and usability features, covering a broad range of use cases from personal desktops to server setups in IoT, cloud, and enterprise environments. Ubuntu is developed and maintained by Canonical Ltd. And benefits from the contributions of a large open-source community. The LTS version is designed to provide long-term stability and support for up to five years from its official release.
